cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Antigravity_Codex_ClaudeCode_DeepSeekHarness: 面向科学计算与工程研发的四客户端配置与验证工具"
message: "If you use this software or workflow specification in academic research or engineering projects, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Xinyu
repository-code: "https://github.com/Xinyu-Li-1997/Antigravity_Codex_ClaudeCode_DeepSeekHarness"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24293507"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24293507
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Shared engineering rules (R0-R11), symmetrical deterministic session lifecycle
  hooks (guarding both overclaimed verification and unverified negative claims),
  read-only review subagents, zero-blacklist lexical grounding and document
  hygiene checks, pre-read sizing and conservative sharding, cross-client
  coverage verification, deterministic mechanical reconciliation tables, and
  cross-client headless verification workflows across Google Antigravity,
  OpenAI Codex, Claude Code, and DeepSeek Harness for scientific computing,
  CAE, CFD, FEA, numerical PDE solvers, HPC, and high-reliability software
  engineering, implemented purely on the Python 3.11+ standard library across
  Windows, WSL2, and Linux.
keywords:
  - scientific-computing
  - computer-aided-engineering
  - computational-fluid-dynamics
  - finite-element-analysis
  - numerical-pde
  - coding-agents
  - verification-harness
  - deterministic-reconciliation
  - documentation-hygiene
  - reproducible-workflows
